The sharpest finding is about the instrument itself. mutants.toml is inert and I verified it rather than repeating CLAUDE.md's claim: it sits at the repo root while current docs put config at `.cargo/mutants.toml, and there is no .cargo/ directory. Every excluded function name has moved — main::collect_multiline is now repl::collect_multiline_rl, main::run_shell_command is now in commands_run.rs, compact_agent/auto_compact_if_needed are in commands_session.rs`. It cannot have matched anything since Day 9. All three readings used `-f` and bypassed it, so it hasn't corrupted a number yet — but it's a config that reads as active governance and governs nothing, in the one subsystem the milestone rests on. Trail of Bits shipped a dedicated agent skill just for mutation-campaign config setup, which is a pointed comment on that.

